Billy's father gave him $10. He spent $1.5 on candy, so he has $10 - $1.5 = $8.5 left. He took half of his change, which is $8.5 / 2 = $4.25. He spent $4.25 on gumballs, which cost $.05 each. He bought 40 gumballs, so he spent $4.25 / 40 = $.10625 on each gumball. Since he spent $4.25 on gumballs, he must have spent $4.25 / $.10625 = 40 pounds of candy.

Final answer: \boxed{40}
